347. Top K Frequent Elements

Given an integer array nums and an integer k, return the k most frequent elements. You may return the answer in any order.  

nums = [1,1,1,2,2,3], k = 2

Generally, we build hashmap, then we solve the problem . 

What if the interviewer ask to solve the problem using min-heap or maximum heap 

Want Largest K Elements?
    Use Min Heap

Want Smallest K Elements?
    Use Max Heap 

Python has default min-heap method only that mean it store largest element, elminated least element , popup smallest elements. 
Python doesn't have max-heap , it stores larger elements at top, instead that we use -negative frequencies storing the values in heap. 
Solve the Problem 

import heapq --> defines the heapq functions to access the methods inside it 

heap = [] --> denotes generall list 

heapq.headpush(heap , (frequencies , number)) 

headpush -- method of pushing element into the list 
heapq -- list 
